  "Partitions": {
    "atom_to_list/1": "Atom name is a valid scalar sequence of at most255 characters. Enumerate Unicode scalars into fresh Cons cells with immediate integer codepoints in order; empty name returns nil. Nonatom arguments raise native badarg. No atom-table change.",
    "atom_to_binary/1": "Default UTF8 conversion delegates to the same name binary as the two-argument UTF8 primitive. On error, pinned erlang.erl catches error and re-raises with original argument list, error_info literal and error_with_info source location; caller/depth behavior is preserved.",
    "atom_to_binary/2": "Validate atom and utf8/unicode/latin1 encoding. UTF8/unicode and ASCII Latin1 return the same immutable per-registered-name UTF8 binary. Non-ASCII Latin1 requires every codepoint<=255 and allocates a fresh transcoded binary. Invalid inputs/encoding raise native badarg. No new atom is created.",
    "list_to_existing_atom/1": "Require a proper list of at most255 valid Unicode scalar integers and an already registered exact name. Every malformed/overlong/absent name raises native badarg; return the existing atom word on success without registration. Exact ordinal scalar identity, no normalization.",
    "binary_to_existing_atom/1": "Default UTF8 existing-name lookup has the same complete validation/lookup as arity2, with the actual source wrapper catch/re-raise metadata and original single argument on errors. No new name is registered.",
    "binary_to_existing_atom/2": "Require a whole-byte bitstring, supported encoding, at most255 decoded valid scalars and exact existing name. Latin1 maps bytes directly; UTF8/unicode reject invalid/noncanonical sequences and scalar/length violations. Return the existing atom word, else badarg. No name creation."
  },
  "CacheInvariant": "One immutable UTF8 binary per exact registered name; its key set is a subset of the bounded permanent atom-name table. Concurrent GetOrAdd returns the published entry; non-ASCII Latin1 remains fresh.",
  "SharedErrorInfoLiteral": "One cached immutable module=erl_erts_errors map matches the source literal; the existing error_with_info source location is reused because it denotes the very same pinned helper.",
